    <skos:note xml:lang="en">accepted</skos:note>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">"Radioactivity" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. "Radioactivity concentration" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. "Pm" means the element "promethium" and "150Pm" is the isotope "promethium-150" with a half-life of 1.12e-01 days.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">radioactivity_concentration_of_150Pm_in_air</skos:prefLabel>
