    <ns1:authoredOn>2018-02-12 16:53:18.0</ns1:authoredOn>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">"Radioactivity" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. "Radioactivity concentration" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. "Xe" means the element "xenon" and "137Xe" is the isotope "xenon-137" with a half-life of 2.71e-03 days.</skos:definition>
    <dc:identifier>SDN:P07::BNDR0RHQ</dc:identifier>
    <skos:notation>SDN:P07::BNDR0RHQ</skos:notation>
