    <dc:identifier>SDN:P07::MXW76TGX</dc:identifier>
    <skos:notation>SDN:P07::MXW76TGX</skos:notation>
    <ns1:hasCurrentVersion rdf:resource="http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/MXW76TGX/1/"/>
    <ns1:version>1</ns1:version>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The phrase "integral_wrt_X_of_Y" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase "wrt" means "with respect to". "Radioactivity" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. "Radioactivity concentration" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. "Ce" means the element "cerium" and "142Ce" is the isotope "cerium-142" with a half-life of 1.82e+19 days.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
