    <dcterms:date>2009-07-06 15:41:29.0</dcterms:date>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">"Content" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The "atmosphere content" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  The chemical formula for nitric acid is HNO3.</skos:definition>
    <owl:versionInfo>1</owl:versionInfo>
    <dcterms:identifier>SDN:P07::CF12N80</dcterms:identifier>
