    <skos:altLabel></skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The surface called "surface" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. "Content" indicates a quantity per unit area. "Radioactivity" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. "Am" means the element "americium" and "242m2Am" is the metastable state of the isotope "americium-242" with a half-life of 1.62e-07 days.</skos:definition>
    <ns1:authoredOn>2018-02-12 16:53:18.0</ns1:authoredOn>
