    <dc:identifier>SDN:P07::F3JQPSP4</dc:identifier>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">"Radioactivity" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. "Radioactivity concentration" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. "U" means the element "uranium" and "236U" is the isotope "uranium-236" with a half-life of 8.73e+09 days.</skos:definition>
